<title>USA: Kmart stock up on takeover rumors.</title>
<headline>Kmart stock up on takeover rumors.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Kmart Corp. rose in heavy trading Tuesday on speculation that the retailer is in takeover talks with the buyout firm Kohlberg Kravis &amp; Roberts.</p>
<p>In late afternoon trading, Kmart was up $1.375 at $11 on volume of nearly 9 million shares, making the stock the most active issue on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Kmart officials were not available for comment and a spokesman for KKR declined to comment.</p>
<p>Several Kmart officials were in New York for the Wednesday opening of another store in New York city.</p>
<p>A trading source in New York cited the market speculation for Kmart's stock rise.</p>
